.TH BOOT 3
.SH NAME
boot \- the running kernel as a file, and its command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B bind -a #B /dev

.B /dev/bootimage
.B /dev/bootargs
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Boot
serves two read-only files describing the kernel that is running.
.PP
.B Bootimage
is the kernel image, byte for byte as it was loaded: its length and
contents are those of the file it was booted from.
Installing the running kernel on the card therefore needs no mechanism
of its own:
.IP
.EX
cp /dev/bootimage /n/dos/tryboot.img
.EE
.PP
It is a snapshot, not live memory.
The image executes where it was loaded, so its data segment changes
for as long as the machine is up; what is served is a copy of that
segment taken at the top of the kernel's entry, before any C code has
written to it, with the text and read-only data taken in place.
.PP
.B Bootargs
is the kernel command line, followed by a newline:
the contents of
.B cmdline.txt
(or, for a trial boot,
.BR tryboot.cmd )
as the Raspberry Pi's firmware reports it; under QEMU's
.B virt
machine, the
.B bootargs
property of the device tree's
.B /chosen
node, which is what
.B -append
sets.
It is empty, but for the newline, when there is none.
The words the kernel itself looks for are listed in
.BR /docs/BAREMETAL.md .
.SH EXAMPLE
Install the running kernel as a candidate and try it once (Raspberry Pi):
.IP
.EX
cp /dev/bootimage /n/dos/tryboot.img
echo tryboot > /dev/sysctl
.EE
.PP
The candidate boots under a watchdog.
From its own shell, keep it with
.IP
.EX
mv /n/dos/tryboot.img /n/dos/infernode8.img
.EE
.PP
or reject it by rebooting.
Never copy over
.BR infernode8.img ,
which is the kernel known to work.
.SH SOURCE
.B /os/arm64/devboot.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR cons (3),
.IR osinit (8)
.br
.B /docs/BAREMETAL.md
.SH HISTORY
The device of this name in Inferno's other native kernels serves
.BR boot ,
.B kexec
and
.BR mem ,
for jumping to an address or a new image and for reading kernel memory.
None of those is here: this kernel is replaced through the file system
and a reset, and its memory is not a file.
